			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1033,
				14
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Remove deprecated Electron polyfill shims\n\nDelete the obsolete Electron-specific polyfill files from Source/Polyfills and Target/Polyfills directories. These shims (ChildProcessPolyfill, FileProtocolShim, FileSystemPolyfill, IPCRendererShim, NativeModulePolyfill, ProcessPolyfill, SharedProcessProxy) were used for the Electron-based VS Code substrate.\n\nAs Land transitions from Electron to Tauri/Rust, these polyfills are no longer needed. The corresponding functionality is now handled by Mountain's native Rust implementations or Tauri APIs. This cleanup completes the migration started in the previous commit which redirected Output imports to Configuration/Polyfill.",
			"SHA": "ebc2366fd587601edc485b936c2d32b5d7400160"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T04:48:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				39
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Rename environment variables and global debug hooks\n\nSimplify naming conventions across the Wind codebase:\n- Rename PostHog environment variables: LAND_POSTHOG_* → {Authorize,Beam,Report,Replay,Ask,Brand}\n- Rename dev logging global: __LAND_DEV_LOG → __Trace (window property and localStorage key)\n- Update Output import paths from Polyfill/* to Configuration/Polyfill/* matching new Output directory structure\n\nAll import re-exports from @codeeditorland/output now resolve through the corrected paths. The tsconfig.json path alias was updated from '../Output/Target/Microsoft/VSCode/*' to '../Output/*' to accommodate the new Output structure.",
			"SHA": "0f4119bbf2a48ffdfa6b3206bab780a98426b5e4"
		},
